---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Home">
  <section class="hero">
    <div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> A PERSONAL ENGINEERING LAB</p><h1>Build it.<br />Understand it.<br /><em>Make it better.</em></h1><p class="lead">DrakeLabs is a place for the systems I run, the things I build, and everything I learn along the way.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={`${base}projects/`}>Explore the projects <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${base}infrastructure/`}>Inside the lab →</a></div></div>
    <div class="blueprint" aria-label="Conceptual view of the DrakeLabs portfolio: infrastructure, projects and journal. This is not a live system monitor."><div class="blueprint-top"><span>THE LAB / AT A GLANCE</span><span>01 — 03</span></div><div class="orbit"><div class="orbit-inner"></div><span class="orbit-label">DRAKE<br /><b>LABS</b></span><span class="satellite one">01 / SYSTEMS</span><span class="satellite two">02 / PROJECTS</span><span class="satellite three">03 / FIELD NOTES</span></div><div class="blueprint-bottom"><span>BUILD → OBSERVE → REFINE</span><span>CONCEPT MAP</span></div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE WORKBENCH</p><h2>From services to stories.</h2></div><p>Built around ownership, reuse, and a shared family library.</p></div><div class="cards"><a class="card" href={`${base}infrastructure/`}><span class="number">01 / INFRASTRUCTURE</span><h3>The systems underneath.</h3><p>A family media system guided by low cost, open-source tools, one interface, and secure access.</p><span class="card-link">Explore the architecture ↗</span></a><a class="card" href={`${base}projects/`}><span class="number">02 / PROJECTS</span><h3>Ideas made tangible.</h3><p>A growing collection of builds, experiments, and lessons from making things work.</p><span class="card-link">Open the project shelf ↗</span></a><a class="card" href={`${base}journal/`}><span class="number">03 / JOURNAL</span><h3>Leave a useful trail.</h3><p>Notes on tradeoffs, discoveries, and what to try next. Written as the lab evolves.</p><span class="card-link">Read the field notes ↗</span></a></div></section>
  <section class="section two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">BEYOND THE LAB</p><h2>Enterprise collaboration.<br />Practical curiosity.</h2></div><div><p>I’m Zachary Drake. My professional work centers on unified communications and contact center technology. DrakeLabs shows how I keep learning, from Linux and containers to designing services my family can use.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}professional/`}>Explore my professional background →</a></div></section>
  <section class="note-strip"><span class="eyebrow">CURRENT CHAPTER</span><h2>Giving the lab a home.</h2><p>DrakeLabs brings the projects, decisions, and lessons together in one place. Explore the story, follow the work on GitHub, or check service availability.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}about/`}>Meet DrakeLabs →</a></section>
</Layout>
